**Finding: MISSING** (LOL-CAP, critical)

The Site Development and Hosting Agreement contains **no limitation of liability provision at all**. Targeted searches for "liability", "liable", "damages", "consequential", "loss", "indemnif" and "aggregate" surfaced only:

- **10.2 No Joint Venture** — "liability" used only in the agency/partnership disclaimer sense;
- **4.2 Termination Payment** — "aggregate Net Sales" in a pricing formula.

Section 9 (Warranties) is limited to corporate authority reps and the Globix carve-out, and Section 10 (General Provisions) runs from Notices to Headings with no cap or damages waiver. So both parties are exposed to unlimited direct *and* consequential damages — this fails even the fallback position (mutual 12-month fee cap with core carve-outs).

**Redline proposed and validated (ok:true)** — new Section 10.9 inserted after p0070, inside the General Provisions block (which survives for two years under 10.7):

- Mutual cap: greater of (a) amounts paid or payable by the Company to HDI under Section 3 in the preceding 12 months and (b) USD 1,000,000;
- Mutual exclusion of indirect/consequential/punitive damages;
- "Excluded Claims" uncapped: confidentiality/data protection/security, indemnification, gross negligence, wilful misconduct, fraud, and IP infringement;
- Company's payment obligations under Sections 3 and 4.2 expressly outside the cap, so the Termination Payment stays fully enforceable.

Note on the cap base: fees here are the 30% revenue-share payments under Section 3, so the 12-month measure is meaningful rather than illusory; the USD 1,000,000 floor guards against low-volume periods.
